cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use FinBoundBench, please cite it as follows."
title: "FinBoundBench: Benchmarking Purpose-Selective AI in Financial Decision Systems"
abstract: >-
  FinBoundBench is a paired benchmark that measures purpose-selective AI in
  financial decision systems: authorized utility retention and prohibited
  influence relative to a model's natural-decision floor. It ships a
  preregistered, frozen, independently re-computed confirmatory study across
  two model families and two financial tasks.
authors:
  - name: "The FinBoundBench Organizing Committee"
date-released: 2026-08-09
keywords:
  - purpose limitation
  - data minimization
  - financial AI
  - LLM governance
  - benchmarking
  - decision influence
license: "pending organizers' choice (see RELEASE_NOTES.md)"
